  A column with no type evidence has the type `unknown`.
  `null` claims a column can hold NULL. ichnos never claims NOT NULL.
  `complete: true` means the declarations list every column.
  A table with no `kind` may list only some of its columns.
  The schema `report` holds the reports, which are queries, not tables.
